The table structure information is (table names): 
['countries', 'customers', 'promotions', 'products', 'times', 'channels', 'sales', 'costs', 'supplementary_demographics', 'currency']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables, columns & possible conditions
------------------------------------------------
sales.amount_sold: value used to measure sales  
sales.quantity_sold: alternative volume metric  
sales.promo_id: filter promo_id = 999  
sales.time_id: join to times; pick the two quarters  
sales.prod_id: identify individual products  

customers.cust_id: join to sales  
customers.country_id: link to countries (keep United States)  
customers.cust_city: aggregate at city level  

countries.country_name / country_id: find the id for “United States”  
times.calendar_quarter_id: pick Q4‑2019 (=1772) & Q4‑2020 (=1776)  
times.time_id: join to sales rows  

Typical fixed conditions that will re‑appear  
• sales.promo_id = 999  
• countries.country_name = 'United States'        -- or LIKE 'United States%'  
• times.calendar_quarter_id IN (1772,1776)        -- Q4‑2019 & Q4‑2020  


Ten explorative → final SQL queries
-----------------------------------

```sql
-- 1.  United States rows in countries – to discover its country_id
SELECT DISTINCT country_id, country_name 
FROM   countries
WHERE  country_name LIKE 'United States%';
```

```sql
-- 2.  Sample of U.S. customers (limit 20)
SELECT DISTINCT cust_id, cust_city, country_id
FROM   customers
WHERE  country_id IN (
       SELECT country_id FROM countries WHERE country_name LIKE 'United States%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Distinct U.S. cities that have at least one customer
SELECT DISTINCT cust_city
FROM   customers
WHERE  country_id IN (
       SELECT country_id FROM countries WHERE country_name LIKE 'United States%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Show the two quarter‑codes we need in the times table
SELECT DISTINCT calendar_quarter_id, calendar_quarter_desc, calendar_year
FROM   times
WHERE  calendar_quarter_id IN (1772,1776);
```

```sql
-- 5.  Raw sales rows for Q4‑2019, promo 999, U.S. customers
SELECT  s.*
FROM    sales   AS s
JOIN    customers AS c   ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN    countries AS co  ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN    times     AS t   ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
WHERE   co.country_name LIKE 'United States%'
  AND   s.promo_id = 999
  AND   t.calendar_quarter_id = 1772
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Raw sales rows for Q4‑2020, promo 999, U.S. customers
SELECT  s.*
FROM    sales   AS s
JOIN    customers AS c   ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN    countries AS co  ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN    times     AS t   ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
WHERE   co.country_name LIKE 'United States%'
  AND   s.promo_id = 999
  AND   t.calendar_quarter_id = 1776
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  City‑level totals in Q4‑2019 (amount_sold)
SELECT  c.cust_city,
        SUM(s.amount_sold) AS sales_2019
FROM    sales   AS s
JOIN    customers AS c   ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN    countries AS co  ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN    times     AS t   ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
WHERE   co.country_name LIKE 'United States%'
  AND   s.promo_id = 999
  AND   t.calendar_quarter_id = 1772
GROUP BY c.cust_city
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  City‑level totals in Q4‑2020 (amount_sold)
SELECT  c.cust_city,
        SUM(s.amount_sold) AS sales_2020
FROM    sales   AS s
JOIN    customers AS c   ON c.cust_id = s.cust_id
JOIN    countries AS co  ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN    times     AS t   ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
WHERE   co.country_name LIKE 'United States%'
  AND   s.promo_id = 999
  AND   t.calendar_quarter_id = 1776
